.TH CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_DECLARE 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_event_loop_declare \- declare an uninitialised ccol_event_loop variable
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_event_loop_declare(name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro expands to `ccol_event_loop name`. It does not initialise
the variable. You must assign the variable before you use it. Use
ccol_event_loop_construct(), or a ccol_event_loop_create*() call.

This macro exists so that the names match those of the other
c_collections modules. Compare it with ctpool_declare().
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name  Variable name to declare.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ccol_event_loop_declare(loop);
char *err = NULL;
loop = ccol_event_loop_create(32, 1, 1, &err);
if (!loop) { fprintf(stderr, "%s\en", err); exit(1); }
/* ... register selectables ... */
ccol_event_loop_destroy(loop);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_event_loop_declare_scoped (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_construct (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_create (3)
